    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32220" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octōphŏron</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">octăph-</span></b> ),
		i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀκτὠφορον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a litter carried by eight bearers</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hominem portare octophoro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Q. Fr. 2, 10, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 43</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 6,
				84, 1</span></i>.—Apposition: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lecticā octophoro ferebatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 11, § 27</span></i>
			; cf. Becker, Gallus, 3, p. 6 (2d ed.).</div>
